The built-in packs in packs/ are written by hand from publicly documented API facts
(endpoint paths, field names, error codes, status values and documented test values).
They do not contain copies of any provider's documentation text. The following
openly licensed API descriptions were used as references:

  Stripe OpenAPI description        https://github.com/stripe/openapi                  MIT License, Copyright (c) Stripe, Inc.
  Twilio OpenAPI description        https://github.com/twilio/twilio-oai               MIT License, Copyright (c) Twilio, Inc.
  GitHub REST API description       https://github.com/github/rest-api-description     MIT License, Copyright (c) GitHub, Inc.
  Resend OpenAPI description        https://github.com/resend/resend-openapi           MIT License, Copyright (c) Resend
  Paystack OpenAPI description      https://github.com/PaystackOSS/openapi             MIT License, Copyright (c) Paystack
  OpenAI OpenAPI description        https://github.com/openai/openai-openapi           MIT License, Copyright (c) OpenAI

The Anthropic pack is written by hand from facts in Anthropic's public API reference
(https://docs.anthropic.com/en/api); it contains no copied documentation text.

registry/official.json lists links to API descriptions that providers publish
themselves. It contains links only, no copies; the descriptions are downloaded to
the user's machine at runtime and keep their owners' licences, which the tool shows.

API descriptions fetched at runtime (for example from the APIs.guru directory, which
is published under CC0 1.0) are downloaded to the user's machine and are not
redistributed by this project. They remain subject to their owners' terms.

